.\" Man page for fcitx5-ainput
.TH ainput 1 "2026-07-28" "0.1.0" "fcitx5-ainput"
.SH NAME
fcitx5\-ainput \- voice input addon for fcitx5
.SH SYNOPSIS
fcitx5 addon, loaded automatically. No standalone binary.
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBfcitx5\-ainput\fP is a push-to-talk voice input addon for the fcitx5
input method framework. It captures audio via PulseAudio, performs
speech recognition through configurable ASR backends, and commits the
recognized text to the active application.

Hold \fBCapsLock\fP to start recording, release to stop and transcribe.
The recognized text is committed at the cursor position.
.PP
The input panel shows \fBlistening\fP, \fBprocessing audio\fP, and
\fBrecognizing\fP status. Network, service, timeout, microphone, and
no-speech failures are shown in that panel and are never inserted into the
application document.
.SH USAGE
.TP
\fBCapsLock\fP (long-press, default 300ms)
Start voice recording. Release to stop and transcribe.
.PP
Recording can start while an earlier cloud request is still recognizing.
Ainput preserves recording and commit order and targets the input context that
was active at the start of each recording. At most three recognitions,
including the active one, are queued. A newer recording is discarded with an
input-panel error when that limit is reached.
.TP
\fBCtrl+CapsLock\fP
Enter provider/denoiser switching mode. The notification shows the
provider's display name with the currently configured model (for example
\fBQwen · qwen-audio-3.1-asr-flash\fP, \fBDoubao · bigmodel\fP, or
\fBZipformer · <model-dir> (local)\fP), read from the provider's config
file. While holding CapsLock:
.br
\fB\(<- / h\fP  \-\- previous ASR provider
.br
\fB\(-> / l\fP  \-\- next ASR provider
.br
\fB\(ua / k\fP   \-\- previous denoiser
.br
\fB\(da / j\fP   \-\- next denoiser
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration files are stored in \fB~/.config/ainput/\fP.
Defaults are built into the code: files are optional and sparse.
Every file supports // line comments.
\fBconfig.json\fP, \fBqwen.json\fP and \fBdoubao.json\fP self-heal:
whenever a read finds them missing, a commented template is regenerated
(mode 0600) -- rename one away to get a fresh template. Seeded credentials
carry a PASTE_YOUR_KEY_HERE placeholder that counts as not configured. Every provider config is re-read
before each recognition; model and parameter changes apply on the next
recording without restarting fcitx5.
Every file is validated on read: JSON syntax errors (with byte offset) are
shown in the input panel and the file's values are not trusted; unknown
fields get a "did you mean" suggestion and type mismatches are named in the
fcitx5 log and the provider switch notification.
.SS Global
.TP
\fBconfig.json\fP
Active provider selection and shared tuning. \fBCtrl+CapsLock\fP switching
rewrites the \fBprovider\fP line, so it always shows the backend the next
login starts with.
.RS
.nf
{
    // qwen | doubao | zipformer | fire_red | mock
    "provider": "qwen",
    "ui":    { "activation_msec": 300 },
    "audio": { "denoise": "speexdsp", "crest_threshold": 0 }
}
.fi
.RE
.SS User-facing (must edit)
.TP
\fBdoubao.json\fP
API credentials for ByteDance Volcengine ASR plus model and timeout tuning.
Submit and result polling share one deadline, \fBtimeout_sec\fP (default 90).
.RS
.nf
{"api_key": "xxx", "resource_id": "volc.seedasr.auc"}
.fi
.RE
.TP
\fBqwen.json\fP
API key, ASR model, and recognition options for Alibaba DashScope
(Qwen-Audio ASR). The model defaults to
\fBqwen-audio-3.1-asr-flash\fP and is configurable via the \fBmodel\fP key.
.RS
.nf
{"api_key": "sk-xxx"}
.fi
.RE
.TP
\fBqwen.json\fP optional keys include \fBmodel\fP, \fBlanguage_hints\fP,
\fBvocabulary\fP, \fBvocabulary_id\fP, \fBkeep_dialect\fP,
\fBspeaker_diarization\fP and \fBtimeout_sec\fP; see
/usr/share/doc/fcitx5-ainput/config/ for commented examples.
.SS Optional (all defaults in code)
.TP
\fBzipformer.json\fP
Local Zipformer tuning: \fBmodel_dir\fP, \fBbin_path\fP, \fBtimeout_sec\fP.
.TP
\fBfire_red.json\fP
Local FireRed tuning: \fBmodel_dir\fP, \fBbin_path\fP, \fBtimeout_sec\fP.
.SH ASR PROVIDERS
.TP
\fBMock\fP
Returns "hello world" immediately. For testing without network.
.TP
\fBZipformer\fP (sherpa-onnx)
Local offline model (~100MB). Requires \fBsherpa-onnx\fP binary.
.TP
\fBFireRed\fP (sherpa-onnx-offline)
Local offline AED model (~1.2GB). Requires \fBsherpa-onnx-offline\fP binary.
.TP
\fBDoubao\fP (ByteDance Volcengine)
Cloud API. Requires \fBdoubao.json\fP with API key and resource ID.
.TP
\fBQwen\fP (Alibaba DashScope)
Cloud API. Requires \fBqwen.json\fP with API key.
.SH AUDIO PIPELINE
Recorded audio goes through:
.RS
.nf
PulseAudio capture
  \(-> ebur128 loudness normalization (-16 LUFS)
  \(-> denoising (speexdsp or deepfilter)
  \(-> VAD-based silence trimming
  \(-> WAV output
  \(-> ASR recognition
.fi
.RE
.PP
PulseAudio capture is asynchronous. On CapsLock release, Ainput returns
control to fcitx5 immediately, retains a short audio tail, then starts
processing and recognition.
.SH RELIABILITY
Doubao and Qwen use persistent serialized workers, allowing curl connections
to be reused while preserving result order. Zipformer and FireRed intentionally
run one local process per utterance.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ainput/
Configuration directory.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ainput/pa_buffer.json
Auto-detected PulseAudio buffer size (created automatically).
.TP
.I /usr/lib/fcitx5/ainput.so
Addon shared library.
.TP
.I /usr/share/fcitx5/addon/ainput.conf
Addon manifest.
.SH BUGS
Report issues at the project repository.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fcitx5 (1)
